        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "084dffdd1ed71c4cf42624b10ad9bb014df5921b",
        "summary": "American Astronomical Society warned that satellites could disrupt research, while others raised concerns about orbital debris and environmental risks Astronomers are pushing back against Elon Musk’s Starmind program to place a huge number of AI computers in space, which was given the green light to proceed by federal communications regulators earlier this week. The American Astronomical Society said it was “disheartened and dismayed” by the decision by the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) decision to grant SpaceX a license to deploy as many as 1m satellites in low Earth orbit as a way of moving datacenters into space.",
